WEBVTT

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.620
Don't pout like that.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.640
I had a reason for punching him.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.880
Even if you don't understand, Joe does.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.810
But that was too cruel, even if it was to teach him boxing!

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.640
He has to fight Rikiishi next week, you know!

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:37.240
Yeah!

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:38.440
What kind of teaching is that!?

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.390
Yeah!

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.240
I had to do it.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.440
There was no other way...

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.870
He had to learn and feel it with his entire body.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.220
Joe!

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.260
Do you understand, Joe?

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.060
That's the foolproof punch to defeat Rikiishi!

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.660
That's the punch for the Sake of Tomorrow!

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:33.480
{hidari daze}Get his left!

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.630
Go, go!

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.130
There! Right there!

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:43.010
From the looks of it, there's no doubt he'll beat everyone, eh?

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.310
What?

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.140
Don't joke around!

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:48.150
Don't you know how intense my fighting style is?

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.260
For the sake of tomorrow...

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:18.880
That fight is for the sake of tomorrow.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:28.080
I guess I was just hearing things.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:30.630
Hey, Joe.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.470
You've been here for three days already.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:35.640
Why won't you tell me what's going on?

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.070
It's unbearable when you're this quiet!

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.070
Hey, Joe, anything is fine! Just stop ignoring me!

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.030
Shut up, you pig.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:51.510
What, you <i>can</i> talk!?

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.190
I almost thought you were dead!

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:55.480
Back off!

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.170
What's wrong, Joe!?

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.130
What, Joe? What're you doing!?

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.090
I can do whatever I want!

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.100
Joe. Joe!

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.950
What's with that face?

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.330
Are you saying you want to try me?

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.100
All right.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.050
I'll take you on!

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:16.590
What're you doing!?

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:19.650
That hurt!

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.350
Yeah.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:23.270
So this is what you look like when you're angry.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.070
Are you crying already?

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.160
What, Joe!?

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.130
What's wrong, you coward? Don't tell me you're scared.

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:31.700
What's wrong?

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.130
Come on!

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.840
Come, take a swing!

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:35.620
Come on!

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.640
What's going on?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.650
H-How did this happen?

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:07.610
I'm starting to understand the fight for the sake of tomorrow.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.630
So what were you trying to do?

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:16.620
He kindly came to visit you. What made you decide to beat him to a pulp?

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.070
Take some time to repent!

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:26.240
At this rate, we can't guarantee that you'll ever be let out of here.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.440
Nishi, sorry,

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.830
but I had to.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.180
No matter how much I upset him, he still saw me as a friend.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:41.480
He wouldn't throw a serious punch at me.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.480
You're still talking about that?

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:48.490
But that's meaningless.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.490
I have to figure out the real trick behind it.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.470
Yabuki, have you gone insane?

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.300
W-We should just throw him in solitary!

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.460
Watch out, guys.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:03.220
If you come too close, I'll bite!

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.560
That's it, this guy's going to solitary!

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:08.280
Come on!

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:10.270
Let go!

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:11.020
Hey!

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:11.920
Let go!

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:16.500
Watch out!

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:21.720
Th-That's Yabuki!

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:23.560
Joe!

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:25.150
What's he doing?

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.310
Solitary confinement? Yeah, right!

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:29.150
The match is in three days.

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.550
I can't even practice in a place like that.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:32.910
No, thanks!

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.150
Be careful, Yabuki!

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:37.120
What'll you do if you fall!?

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.370
What? I'm just going to practice boxing with the guys down there.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:42.290
Here I go!

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:47.840
H-He did it!

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:49.220
Yabuki!

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.720
Are you okay, Yabuki?

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.230
You might have sprained something.

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:52.900
Don't move!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.220
We'll bring a doctor over, so wait there.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:57.840
Got it? Stay right there!

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.060
Yabuki, don't move!

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:01.730
Huh?

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.280
That jump was nothing!

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.690
See you!

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:10.700
Catch him!

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:12.900
You guys, restrain Yabuki!

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:15.700
Just catch me if you can!

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:16.710
Move, move!

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.010
Everyone, move!

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.880
Hurry and capture Yabuki!

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.310
We'll give three days of break to whoever catches him!

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.230
Catch him!

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:26.500
All right!

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.650
Let's do it!

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:28.580
Stop right there!

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.210
You've got no chance!

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:31.470
I've got this!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.760
Wait!

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:42.870
Wait!

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.400
Hey, wait!

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:50.400
How terrible.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:54.210
Joe found a great punch.

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:57.370
I get the shivers just remembering it.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.370
That really gets to me.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:03.290
Every time Joe learns a punch,

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:07.380
it seems like he becomes a little more heartless.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:10.620
Why do I feel like that's happening?

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:16.390
I don't know what's happening, but it really, really bothers me!

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:19.890
What? Did you find Yabuki?

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.540
Did you catch him?

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:23.890
Not yet.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.110
Wh-What?

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:27.900
Then what about the inmates who went after him?

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:31.460
W-Well, they've all...

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.860
they've all been taken down!

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:39.260
Hey, hey!

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:40.870
What's wrong? Get a hold of yourself!

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:46.710
I caught up to him, and just as I was about to punch,

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.530
he suddenly turned around...

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:50.650
Hey!

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.210
Hang in there! Hey!

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.880
This is the first victim.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:57.890
Come, this way!

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.350
Hurry!

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.130
Yabuki!

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:24.410
This guy's hopeless.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.580
We can't do anything.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:31.770
Rikiishi! H-Help us out!

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:34.790
Can you restrain that troublemaker?

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.340
Oh, don't say that.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:38.960
Wait a little bit.

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:42.570
If I take him down now,

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:46.600
it'll spoil Sunday's boxing match.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:52.710
Just hold on for a little longer.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:55.450
I'll make sure he'll never be able to do this again.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:56.640
And I do mean "never."

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.610
I don't get what you mean.

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.040
I don't understand.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:02.610
What happened?

00:10:03.590 --> 00:10:05.620
What is it, Nomura-san?

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.700
Well, this is weird.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:10.630
The first and second victims were still conscious when we found them,

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:15.130
but everyone here has completely lost consciousness.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.500
Which means...

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:20.140
Which means... what exactly?

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:26.420
If an individual uses all of his strength fighting, he'll get tired after a while.

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:28.620
You'd normally expect less damage to be done as time passes by,

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.100
but this is completely the opposite.

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:37.420
So are you saying the more Yabuki punched, the stronger his punches became?

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.180
Well, that seems to be the case.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:41.360
Anyway, I can't believe a human did this.

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:44.120
The more he punches, the stronger he gets?

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:51.620
Oh, if it isn't Rikiishi!

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.630
What're you spacing out for?

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.650
Hey, Rikiishi, listen up.

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:02.640
I was just thinking how great it would be if our match was today.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.280
How about it? Know what I'm saying?

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:15.060
This guy...

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:17.850
What kind of punch did he learn?

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:38.320
If I remember correctly, that coach was standing by the pillar over there.

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:43.550
Yabuki took that punch and fell over,

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.050
but...

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:49.090
The old man coughed up blood and fell over, too.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:51.770
Something must have happened.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.480
Something...

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.080
This is...

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:07.630
I know what punch he's using.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:08.580
I see.

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.830
That darn old coach.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.780
He taught him a monstrous punch.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:21.980
Hey.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.130
What's he doing?

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:51.640
Rikiishi-san, what're you doing?

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:53.180
They'll run wild!

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:56.460
Rikiishi-san, watch out!

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:57.370
Run!

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:47.110
He's skipping out on work, and is practicing all day.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.190
The supervisors are gonna find out about this!

00:13:50.980 --> 00:13:55.170
No matter how much he practices, Rikiishi-san will get him and he'll be all:

00:13:55.170 --> 00:14:01.190
"Crunch, crunchie, cruncho, into bits and pieces!"

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:01.190
<i>Hey, skeleton boy.</i>

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:04.690
Did you just say something?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.900
I-I didn't say anything!

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:12.030
How about it? Instead of all this work, how about sparring with me for a bit?

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.900
I'll fix your face a bit for you.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:16.790
Don't kid with me!

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:18.920
I don't want any m-more of those punches!

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.440
Don't worry.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:25.840
A little squirt like you wouldn't even count as practice for me.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.840
Now, time to do some work.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:31.860
Yo, Nishi.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.670
What's up?

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:36.720
Did you already finish up at the animal barn?

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:37.430
Yeah.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:39.140
What?

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.220
Why do you look so down?

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.410
Joe, it's huge.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:49.550
Rikiishi's doing some terrifying practice for the match tomorrow!

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:51.950
What?

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:53.280
Of all things I thought you'd say...

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:56.790
Hey, hey! What's this about Rikiishi-san's practice?

00:14:57.460 --> 00:14:58.420
So what is it?

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:01.750
Is he working out to prepare for my punches?

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.890
That's not unusual.

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:05.600
That's not it! Bulls!

00:15:05.600 --> 00:15:07.760
He's fighting bulls!

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:09.660
Bulls?

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:11.930
Move it, move!

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.760
Come on, move!

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:14.970
We need to get him to the vet!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:15.470
Yes!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:16.810
Everyone, move!

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:30.760
He completely beat two of them unconscious.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.040
Amazing...

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.390
I've got the shivers.

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:39.750
I heard he did it in one blow.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:43.500
Yeah, if a human took that, they wouldn't live to talk about it.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.440
It happens in a flash.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:52.720
With this, I'm really looking forward to Rikiishi-san's match tomorrow.

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:57.720
Hey, Joe, this must be Rikiishi's response to your punch!

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.290
What're you gonna do, Joe?

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:02.920
Shut up!

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:04.500
Stop blabbering!

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.290
You're not on Rikiishi's side, are you?

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.230
Joe!

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:29.740
Yo, Yabuki.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.590
Your bravado ends today.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:43.140
I wanted to show you how I'd destroy your stupid "for the Sake of Tomorrow" punch.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.650
Well, to me, it's just another troublesome obstacle;

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:54.020
the fact that I'm worrying that I'll really punch you to death tomorrow.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:58.610
Well, if that happens, it won't be a fight, it'll be a match.

00:16:58.610 --> 00:16:59.780
See ya.

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:35.120
Thank you so much for the wonderful ring.

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.160
Thank you so much.

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:40.250
Rikiishi-kun looks well.

00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:45.260
Yes, as expected of your ex-pro boxer.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:47.120
He's completely ready.

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:53.760
All right, I'm fully prepared now.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:56.460
Look at that, Rikiishi-san is great, as expected.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:59.640
When I see that stance, he really stands out in the crowd!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:03.770
That Yabuki won't stand a chance against him!

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:06.480
Look at him.

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:09.020
He's just been sitting there thinking and doing nothing this whole time.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.730
It's too late to regret it.

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:14.570
Rikiishi-san should just punch that guy to oblivion!

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:18.600
What're you doing over there?

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:21.420
It's almost time for your bed-time in the ring!

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:22.780
Come this way!

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:29.570
Bro Joe! You can do it! Bro Joe! You can do it!

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.350
Bro Joe! You can do it!

00:18:31.350 --> 00:18:31.790
Joe—

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:34.260
There he is! Joe!

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:35.170
Joe!

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:37.000
Bro Joe, we're here to root for you.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:38.760
How are you doing?

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:40.260
Yeah.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:41.650
"Yeah," he says.

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:43.630
Joe doesn't look too good.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:47.560
Maybe he had diarrhea or something. He looks a bit sickly.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:49.080
What's going on?

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.290
Hey, bro!

00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:51.350
You feeling okay?

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:52.870
Bro!

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:58.390
Now, now, step aside.

00:18:58.390 --> 00:18:59.360
I need to talk to Joe.

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:02.580
Hey, what's wrong? You look down.

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:04.680
Old man.

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:08.540
How strong is that punch "for the Sake of Tomorrow"?

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:13.500
You already mastered that?

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:17.510
I'm asking how strong it is!

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:18.970
I see.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.840
You did it, great!

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.810
With that, you've got nothing to be scared of!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.470
Nothing to be scared of, eh?

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.020
Joe, look.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:33.000
This seems like a good time.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:39.110
They're a bit old, but I'd like you to use these gloves for your debut match.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:39.990
How about it?

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:41.040
They've got a good scent.

00:19:41.040 --> 00:19:43.180
It's the faint smell of blood.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.450
Can you smell it?

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.990
Blood?

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.290
Yes.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:49.990
These gloves...

00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:53.430
Yes, I used these long ago.

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:57.680
I used to bathe these in blood every match.

00:19:57.680 --> 00:20:02.680
Even now, the smell of these gloves makes my blood boil.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:08.990
How about it? Will you use them?

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:10.980
They suit you.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.380
Cheer up.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:15.980
What's gotten into you?

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:22.490
Well, everyone's like that before their debut match.

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:25.490
Shut up for a moment, old man!

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.540
Yo, Yabuki.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.820
I brought you kids' head gear.

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:36.540
You'll need it against Rikiishi-san, after all.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.810
Well, wear it and do your best.

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:44.490
Although it won't change the fact that Rikiishi-san's going to take you down.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:51.720
Save me! Save me!

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:55.220
You keep making fun of people to satisfy yourself!

00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:58.810
You do that again, and I'll tear off whatever's left of your hair!

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:00.750
My hair! My hair!

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:01.820
No!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.160
Well, old man, I'll be borrowing these beat-up gloves.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.660
Yeah, yeah, fine!

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:15.040
Bro!

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:19.670
Everyone, enjoy watching the match.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.310
Joe, do your best!

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:23.670
Don't lose to that big-headed Rikiishi.

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:25.460
Just watch.

00:21:25.460 --> 00:21:29.280
I'll beat him to a complete pulp.

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:30.370
Just wait!

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:34.260
Joe, that's it!

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:35.810
That's the real you!

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:37.650
Move!

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:43.150
You look terrible.

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:45.860
And you box?

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:47.080
Yo, Yabuki.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.160
You've got two bellybuttons, don't you?

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:52.470
That's why he's embarrassed and won't take off his top!

00:21:56.250 --> 00:22:00.100
This is enough for me to beat up that pig, that's all.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:03.130
This guy...

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:07.640
And with that monstrous face, there's only one thing for you.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:12.570
Well, you better start thinking about what to do when you take my punch,

00:22:12.570 --> 00:22:14.140
you big idiot!

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:16.160
Bastard.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.560
Stop, Rikiishi-kun.

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:19.830
Yes, ma'am.

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:24.980
Yabuki-kun, you're ready, right?

00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:28.990
Then you don't mind if we ring the gong, right?

00:22:29.320 --> 00:22:30.310
Yeah!

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:34.990
If you're ready, then ring it whenever you want.

00:22:35.810 --> 00:22:38.640
I've been ready for ages.

00:22:39.510 --> 00:22:41.000
Now, bring it!

00:22:44.530 --> 00:22:46.010
Well said.

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:46.960
Well said, Joe.

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:52.010
Feel anxiety towards your first experience with the terror of boxing.

00:22:52.010 --> 00:22:53.730
You must face and accept those feelings,

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:57.870
but make sure you overcome that anxiety,

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:02.020
and make sure you aim for victory through blood and sweat!

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:03.530
There's no mistake.

00:23:03.530 --> 00:23:07.030
You were born to box.

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:09.590
You've got the blood of a beast!

00:23:09.590 --> 00:23:10.880
Go, Joe!

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:15.050
And... And fight with your life on the line, Joe!

00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:43.310
The gong rings for Joe and Rikiishi.

00:24:44.080 --> 00:24:47.170
As the boxing specialist, Rikiishi's punches are powerful.

00:24:47.170 --> 00:24:49.480
Joe keeps going down.

00:24:49.480 --> 00:24:51.690
Beaten up and covered in blood,

00:24:51.690 --> 00:24:54.630
Joe explodes and uses his foolproof cross counter.

00:24:54.630 --> 00:24:56.200
Which way is tomorrow?
